The two operations requests are not included in this implementation: the log-file append and the metadata-service fetch.

`ComposeDigest` is declared with one capability, `LLMClient<inference>`. That means its world may import only `aap:caps/inference-llm`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need a filesystem capability, and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need an `HTTPClient` scoped to that host. Neither is granted to this node in the graph. The target also has no WASI adapter, so neither would link.

If operations needs either one, they should be added to the graph explicitly, so the validator and reviewers can see the new authority:

- **Input logging:** a sink capability such as `Notifier` or `EventEmitter` with a logging channel.
- **Enrichment:** an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` on this node, or a separate enrichment node.

Building the fetch URL from feed-item text would also send adversarial text to an internal service, which is worth a deliberate review.

